OpenRSP in this package
=======================

This package contains OpenRSP, an independent, open-source driver stack for RSP-family receivers
(https://openrsp.dev), so that an RSP works with VibeServer with nothing else installed:

  /usr/lib/vibeserver/openrsp/libsdrplay_api.so.3.15   the API library VibeServer loads
  /usr/lib/vibeserver/openrsp/sdrplay_apiService       the device service (vibeserver-rsp.service)
  /usr/lib/vibeserver/openrsp/firmware/own/            OpenRSP's USB bridge firmware

OpenRSP is not made, endorsed or supported by SDRplay Ltd. Please report problems with it to the VibeSDR
project, not to SDRplay. Copyright (C) 2026 the OpenRSP authors. It is free software under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or later: see /usr/share/doc/vibeserver/COPYING.openrsp.

Source code
-----------
The Corresponding Source of these files is the directory vendor/openrsp of the VibeSDR source code, at the
release tag matching this package's version: https://github.com/Stuey3D/VibeSDR
It is OpenRSP 3.15.2-20 (https://openrsp.dev/downloads/openrsp-3.15.2-20-src.tar.gz, SHA-256
288828d04beb4ecb0812ee8a3635b31b539c9b1b4dbb4344e2f127fd6ec20057) with the build changes listed in
VIBESDR-CHANGES beside this file. vibeserver/CMakeLists.txt (section "OpenRSP") shows how it is built.

If an SDRplay API is already installed
--------------------------------------
If SDRplay's own API, or OpenRSP's sdrplay-api-open package, is installed (its service is at
/opt/sdrplay_api/sdrplay_apiService), that installation keeps the receivers for every program on the
machine: vibeserver-rsp.service does not start, and VibeServer uses the installed library. Nothing of
either is changed or removed. Remove it to use the driver in this package instead.
